 "intro": "Near Utica in Africa, 203 BC. You are Publius Cornelius Scipio, landed in Africa. Hasdrubal Gisco and King Syphax of the Numidians are camped near you with much larger armies.",
 "debrief": "In Polybius’s account, Scipio used peace talks to send officers disguised as slaves into the enemy camps. He then attacked by night, setting fire to Syphax’s reed huts; when the Carthaginians came to help, unarmed, their camp was fired too, and huge numbers died. A month later, the enemy raised a new army with 4,000 Celtiberians on the Great Plains. Scipio’s cavalry broke the wings, and the principes and triarii wheeled round the Celtiberians, who died fighting. Carthage recalled Hannibal from Italy, and Syphax was captured. The other choices are what-ifs.",
